ould exploit two denial of service (dos) vulnerabilities by providing a specially crafted executable and linkable format (elf) file. one vulnerability, a resource exhaustion (cwe-400), can lead to an out-of-memory condition. the other, a null pointer dereference (cwe-476), can cause a segmentation fault. both issues can result in the `readelf` utility becoming unresponsive or crashing, leading to a denial of service."},{"subject":"CVE-2026-6844","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 10","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat enterprise linux 10"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-6844","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 7","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat enterprise linux 7"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-6844","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 8","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat enterprise linux 8"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-6844","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 9","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat enterprise linux 9"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-6844","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Hardened Images","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat hardened images"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-6844","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat OpenShift AI (RHOAI)","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat openshift ai (rhoai)"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-6844","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat OpenShift Container Platform 4","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat openshift container platform 4"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-6844","predicate":"rdf:type","object":"Vulnerability","source":"cve","object_type":"enum","object_canonical":"vulnerability"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-6844","predicate":"related-weakness","object":"CWE-400","source":"cve","object_type":"id","object_canonical":"CWE-400"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-6844","predicate":"state",